      "standardized_narrative": "Syndicate 2791 experienced a gross back year release of GBP 16.1 million in 2020, primarily driven by favorable claims development across various lines. This included a GBP 5.4 million release from long-tail casualty classes, a GBP 4.5 million release from the short-tail account, and a GBP 6.2 million release from auto and other miscellaneous specialty classes. Specific contributors to the favorable development included positive legal rulings for Superstorm Sandy, a GBP 3.2 million release from a Canadian wildfire reinsurance contract due to arbitration, and better-than-expected performance on the Irish motor account. However, there was also an increase in ultimate gross catastrophe losses for 2017 events (Hurricanes Harvey, Irma, Maria, and Californian Wildfires).",
