        "certain legal rulings have proved more favourable than initially forecast",
        "prevailed in a market-wide arbitration involving a Canadian wildfire reinsurance contract affecting the 2015 year, which enabled a GBP 3.2m release from reserves",
        "roughly 10% deterioration in our gross Irma loss, driven mainly by the catastrophe excess of loss book",
        "dramatic upwards movement in market loss estimates over the last three years",
        "projecting ultimate gross catastrophe losses, after cessions to Syndicate 6103, of $79.2m, (last year $73.7m)",
        "GBP 6.2m gross back-year release, 60% of which was generated by a better than expected performance on the large Irish motor account",
        "positive run-off of GBP 16.1m on the 2017 and prior years' reserves",
        "net surplus in ultimate claims of GBP 6.0m (2019: GBP 24.6m) due to lower than expected incurred movements across most classes of business"
