      "standardized_narrative": "Syndicate 2791 reported a gross release on prior years of GBP 16.1m in the 2020 reporting period (approximately a 5.0% reduction versus opening gross claims outstanding of GBP 322.2m). The release was driven by favourable claims development across both long-tail casualty (c.GBP 5.4m release) and short-tail classes (c.GBP 4.5m), better than expected performance on a large Irish motor account (part of a GBP 6.2m release in auto/specialty classes), and favourable legal/arbitration outcomes (including a GBP 3.2m release from a Canadian wildfire reinsurance arbitration). A small number of older years (notably 2004 and 2014) experienced isolated adverse issues, but overall the movement was a net release.",
      "raw_causal_phrases": [
        "members benefitted from a gross back year release of GBP 16.1m (GBP 16.1m net of reinsurance, before agency profit commission).",
        "There was a gross back year release of GBP 16.1m, and the IBNR reserve for 2018 has been set at GBP 17.8m, meaning the ongoing total gross IBNR reserve is now GBP 118.2m.",
        "The long-tail casualty classes generated a GBP 5.4m gross back-year release, and now constitute 40% of the total remaining IBNR reserve (last year 41%).",
        "The short-tail account generated a GBP 4.5m gross back-year release.",
        "There was a GBP 6.2m gross back-year release, 60% of which was generated by a better than expected performance on the large Irish motor account, which we wrote 2012-16.",
        "we prevailed in a market-wide arbitration involving a Canadian wildfire reinsurance contract affecting the 2015 year, which enabled a GBP 3.2m release from reserves.",
        "A positive run-off of GBP 16.1m on the 2017 and prior years' reserves (2016 and prior: GBP 19.0m) was experienced in the year."
